NUM-32: infiltrate only the ponded water left after evaporation

getSubareaRunoff() charges evaporation to the ponded water first
(surfEvap = MIN(depth/tStep, evap)) and then asks for the infiltration rate
with the full ponded depth, so infiltration can take water that has already
evaporated. When the two together use up the surface water the depth is set
to zero but both full volumes are booked, up to evap x tStep of water that
never existed. Pass the depth left after evaporation to infil_getInfil(), as
the infiltration routines document (net rainfall = rainfall + runon -
evaporation); the infiltration state then advances by the water actually
infiltrated.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-32_swmm530.patch

